{
  "about": "Sample messages and the codes each code style must find in them. The one file every code reader is checked against: core/codes.py (python -m core.codes_check), the Android app's ProductCode.kt (its unit test), the iPhone app's ProductCode.swift (the iOS workflow) and the website's lib/codes.ts (scripts/check-codes.mjs, which reads its copy lib/code_samples.json; python -m core.codes_check --sync-web copies this file there). Change this file first, then the readers. Codes in 'codes' lists are keys: the prefix in lower case, a dash, the number without leading zeros ('2-152', '5a-380', 'cc-1023'); a keyword-style code has no prefix, so its key is the number alone ('1023'). Patterns are tried case-insensitively, as the WhatsApp script uses them.",
